WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了终极版《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're the Office Ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

8
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:24.410
Hello, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.130
Hey, today is a big day, you guys.
嘿，伙计们，今天是个大日子。

10
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.310
This is a very special episode of Office Ladies.
这是非常特别的一期《办公室女士》节目。

11
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.950
We are not breaking down an episode of The Office.
我们今天不剖析《办公室》的剧集。

12
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:33.450
Oh, no.
噢，不。

13
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.210
Well, you better buckle in.
好吧，你们最好系好安全带。

14
00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.150
And we're breaking down Speed.
我们要剖析的是《生死时速》。

15
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.110
Speed with Keanu Reeves and Sandra Bullock, Dennis Hopper, Jeff Daniels.
由基努·里维斯、桑德拉·布洛克、丹尼斯·霍珀和杰夫·丹尼尔斯主演的《生死时速》。

16
00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.130
Lady.
天哪。

17
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.510
I am very excited to break this down.
我非常兴奋能剖析这部电影。

18
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.590
We did a lot of research for this.
我们为此做了大量的研究。

19
00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.510
We have watched Speed more times in a row than I thought I ever would.
我们连续观看《生死时速》的次数比我预想的要多得多。

20
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.370
So much.
多太多了。

21
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:58.450
I was telling Sam and Cassie this last week I've been having a little trouble sleeping.
我上周告诉萨姆和卡西，我最近有点失眠。

22
00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:05.190
I think it is the cortisol from watching these tense bus chase scenes.
我想是因为看了这些紧张的公交车追逐戏，导致皮质醇水平升高了。

23
00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:05.670
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

24
00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.230
For five days and nights.
连续五天五夜。

25
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:07.590
Yeah.
没错。

26
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.650
But I'll tell you one thing.
但我得告诉你一件事。

27
00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:10.650
This movie holds up.
这部电影依然经典。

28
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.530
It really does.
确实如此。

29
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:20.670
I have watched all of these, like, behind-the-scenes, making-of videos where I watched them intricately perform all these stunts as part of my research today.
为了今天的研究，我看了所有幕后制作花絮，仔细观看了他们如何完成这些特技动作。

30
00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.850
And yet when I watch the movie, it's seamless.
然而当我再看电影时，一切都衔接得天衣无缝。

31
00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.870
I am so impressed by this movie.
我对这部电影印象深刻。

32
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.710
I cannot believe the stunts they did and that the actors did them.
我简直不敢相信他们完成的那些特技，而且还是演员亲自上阵。

33
00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.810
We're going to get to it.
我们马上就要讲到了。

34
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.190
Here's the research I did.
这是我做的研究。

35
00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:33.930
Ready, folks?
准备好了吗，各位？

36
00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:34.310
Yes.
准备好了。

37
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.450
Got an old tech alert for you.
有个老派科技提醒要告诉你们。

38
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.290
I got the DVDs with the extras.
我找出了带有花絮的DVD。

39
00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.530
Of course you did.
你当然会这么做。

40
00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.150
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

41
00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.710
Let me tell you what is on this DVD extras because it's worth it.
让我告诉你们这张DVD花絮里有什么，因为非常值得一看。

42
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.510
Audio commentary with the director, Jan de Bont.
导演扬·德·邦特的音频评论。

43
00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.210
Audio commentary with writer, Graham YoSt.
编剧格雷厄姆·约斯特的音频评论。

44
00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.670
And producer, Mark Gordon.
还有制片人马克·戈登的评论。

45
00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.250
Action sequences.
动作场面。

46
00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:56.270
Behind-the-scenes footage and interviews with director and stunt coordinator, Gary Himes.
幕后花絮以及对导演和特技协调员加里·海姆斯采访。

47
00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.150
Behind-the-scenes of all the stunts on the subway train.
地铁列车上所有特技动作的幕后制作。

48
00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:00.890
Inside speed.
深入《生死时速》。

49
00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:05.330
On location, stunts, visual effects, HBO, first look, the making of speed.
外景拍摄、特技、视觉特效、HBO特别节目、抢先看、《生死时速》制作特辑。

50
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.290
Extended scenes, trailers, and TV spots.
加长片段、预告片和电视宣传片。

51
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:09.890
Gallery of photos.
照片画廊。

52
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.190
And a music video by Billy Idol.
还有比利·爱多尔的音乐录影带。

53
00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.730
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

54
00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.550
Your little tiny blonde middle-aged lady watched all of it.
你们这位娇小金发的中年女士把这些全看完了。

55
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.930
I have seen all of this.
我把这些都看过了。

56
00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.510
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

57
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:30.350
Also, you guys, I want you to know, the director, Jan, was a former cinematographer.
另外，各位，我想让你们知道，导演扬以前是位摄影指导。

58
00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.390
He had worked on Hunt for Red October, Die Hard, Basic Instinct, Lethal Weapon 3.
他曾参与过《猎杀红色十月》、《虎胆龙威》、《本能》和《致命武器3》的拍摄。

59
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.810
He would operate the camera himself in this movie a ton.
在这部电影里，他经常亲自操作摄像机。

60
00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.510
Like, handheld camera.
比如，手持摄像机拍摄。

61
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.570
And this was his directorial debut, right?
这是他的导演处女作，对吧？

62
00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.490
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

63
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.670
And he would just grab the camera and be like, guys, I got to get in there.
他会直接抓起摄像机说，伙计们，我得进去拍。

64
00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:48.950
Let me operate this camera.
让我来操作这台摄像机。

65
00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:49.910
He would pull focus.
他会亲自跟焦。

66
00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.670
He would even slate for himself on the bus.
在公交车上，他甚至会自己打板。

67
00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.870
I saw many behind-the-scenes videos.
我看了很多幕后花絮视频。

68
00:02:54.930 --> 00:03:04.770
And he gave an interview where he said they could fit so few people on the bus besides the cast that you kind of had to do more than one job.
他在一次采访中说，除了演员，车上能容纳的人数非常有限，所以你不得不身兼数职。

69
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:05.290
Yeah.
没错。

70
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.650
And so, yeah, he did the clicker and all the things.
所以，是的，他负责打板以及所有杂事。

71
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:08.550
He did all the things.
他什么都干。

72
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:12.030
And he really wanted you to feel like you were in these shots with them.
他真的很想让观众感觉自己和演员们一起身处镜头之中。

73
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.890
So that's why he was up-up in their business with the handheld.
所以他才要用手持摄像机凑得那么近。

74
00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.090
Well, we have one more exciting thing to tell you.
好了，我们还有一件令人兴奋的事情要告诉你们。

75
00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.150
Also, we interviewed Beth Grant.
我们还采访了贝丝·格兰特。

76
00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.890
You know her as Dwight's babysitter and date to the dinner party on the office.
你们可能知道她，她在《办公室》里演德怀特的保姆，还是他参加晚宴时的女伴。

77
00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.990
You guys, she's on the bus.
伙计们，她在车上。

78
00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.210
She's on the bus.
她在车上。

79
00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:33.110
She's the lady who gets blown up trying to get off the bus when she shouldn't.
她就是那个在不该下车时试图下车结果被炸飞的女士。

80
00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:33.430
Yeah.
没错。

81
00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:41.010
So we had the loveliest interview with her, and we are going to release that as a bonus episode in a couple of days.
我们和她进行了一次非常愉快的访谈，我们将在几天后作为特别节目发布。

82
00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.010
It's so good.
非常精彩。

83
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.190
You have to listen to her behind-the-scenes stories.
你们一定要听听她的幕后故事。

84
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.090
We have so much to cover in this speed breakdown that we wanted to give Beth a standalone.
这次《生死时速》的解析内容太多了，所以我们想给贝丝单独做一期节目。

85
00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.470
Should we get started?
我们要开始了吗？

86
00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.070
We better.
最好开始了。

87
00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.930
My document's 45 pages.
我的文档有45页长。

88
00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:53.670
Oh, dear.
天哪。

89
00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:54.390
Here we go.
开始了。

90
00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.370
Buckle in, everyone.
大家系好安全带。

91
00:03:56.070 --> 00:04:03.770
Speed, written by Graham Yost, directed by Jan de Bont, produced by Mark Gordon, with a running time of 116 minutes.
《生死时速》，编剧格雷厄姆·约斯特，导演扬·德·邦特，制片人马克·戈登，片长116分钟。

92
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.030
Here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

93
00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.950
A madman has rigged an L.A.
一个疯子在洛杉矶的公交车上安装了炸弹。

94
00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.770
bus with a bomb.
如果车速降到每小时50英里以下，炸弹就会爆炸，炸死车上所有人。

95
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:14.130
If the bus drops below 50 miles per hour, the bomb will go off, killing everyone on board.
他索要370万美元现金，否则就炸掉公交车。

96
00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.230
He wants $3.7 million in cash, or he's going to blow up the bus.
就是这样。

97
00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:20.730
That's it.
没错。

98
00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:21.010
Yeah.
是的。

99
00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:21.870
It's simple.
很简单。

100
00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:22.530
It's simple.
很简单。

101
00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.410
Fast fact number one.
第一个冷知识。

102
00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.610
Graham Yost said that the original title for this movie was Minimum Speed.
格雷厄姆·约斯特说这部电影最初的片名是《最低限速》。

103
00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:29.230
No.
不。

104
00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:29.950
Yeah.
没错。

105
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:30.930
Minimum Speed.
《最低限速》。

106
00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.170
No, that's not a good...
不，那不是个好……

107
00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:32.590
What?
什么？

108
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.470
You guys, I want you to go the Minimum Speed.
伙计们，我要你们保持“最低限速”。

109
00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:41.550
He said he changed it when he realized it probably wasn't a good idea to have the word minimum in a movie title.
他说当他意识到电影片名里带个“最低”可能不太好时，就改掉了。

110
00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.370
That's so funny.
太搞笑了。

111
00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.310
Graham was a writer on Full House when he wrote this script.
格雷厄姆写这个剧本时是《欢乐满屋》的编剧。

112
00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.290
He was a TV writer.
他是个电视编剧。

113
00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:52.090
He was inspired by the Akira Kurosawa movie, Runaway Train.
他的灵感来源于黑泽明导演的电影《暴走列车》。

114
00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.910
And he thought, well, what if we put a bomb on a bus?
他想，要是我们在公交车上放个炸弹会怎样？

115
00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.910
He wrote this movie on spec.
他写这部电影时并没有预售合同。

116
00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:00.370
That means he wrote it for free in his free time.
这意味着他是利用业余时间免费创作的。

117
00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.990
And then he took it out to the studios and shopped it around.
然后他拿着剧本去各大制片厂推销。

118
00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:10.530
Speed was shot in September of 1993, making this the 30th anniversary of the filming of Speed.
《生死时速》拍摄于1993年9月，所以今年是该片拍摄30周年。

119
00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.910
And we talked to Beth about that, how it's been 30 years.
我们和贝丝聊过这个，说起已经过去30年了。

120
00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:14.910
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

121
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:21.530
Also, I want you guys to know, many people on the commentaries talked about how hot it was.
另外，我想让你们知道，很多评论音轨里的人都提到当时有多热。

122
00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.650
Because September is our hottest month in California.
因为9月是我们加州最热的月份。

123
00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.850
And they were on a freeway in September.
而且他们9月份还在高速公路上。

124
00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.170
On a bus.
在公交车上。

125
00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:28.830
On a bus.
在公交车上。

126
00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:32.150
And then in between scenes, they'd be like on the side of the freeway.
而且在拍摄间隙，他们就待在高速公路边上。

127
00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.050
Yes.
没错。

128
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:38.050
This reminded me of us standing outside in our heavy coats in the Dunder Mifflin parking lot,
这让我想起我们穿着厚外套站在邓德·米夫林停车场的场景，

129
00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.610
pretending like it was winter when really it was so, so hot.
假装是冬天，但实际上热得要命。

130
00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.290
We are just like Speed.
我们简直就像《生死时速》一样。

131
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.730
You and I, we are cast on The Office.
你和我，我们是《办公室》的演员。

132
00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.830
You know what, though?
不过你知道吗？

133
00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.070
All the people are trapped in the bus all the time.
所有人都一直被困在公交车里。

134
00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.030
And it made me think of our conference room scenes.
这让我想到了我们的会议室场景。

135
00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:52.570
I know.
我知道。

136
00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.310
I did think about that.
我也想到了。

137
00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.110
I was like, I get how you get punchy in one room all day.
我当时就在想，我明白为什么整天待在一个房间里会让人变得神经质了。

138
00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:57.510
Yeah.
是啊。

139
00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.570
What if the cast of The Office did a remake of Speed?
如果《办公室》的演员们翻拍《生死时速》会怎样？

140
00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:01.810
Hear me out.
听我说完。

141
00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:03.450
Say no more.
别说了。

142
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.430
Come on.
来吧。

143
00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.010
I'm in.
我加入。

144
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:05.430
Right?
对吧？

145
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.510
This is the reunion no one's thought of.
这就是没人想到的重聚方式。

146
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.210
Dwight is the madman.
德怀特是那个疯子。

147
00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:09.830
Yes.
没错。

148
00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:10.770
Of course.
当然。

149
00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:11.210
Yes.
是的。

150
00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.750
Toby tries to escape.
托比试图逃跑。

151
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.490
He gets killed.
他被杀了。

152
00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.030
Do I get to drive the bus?
我可以开那辆巴士吗？

153
00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.630
You get to drive the bus.
你可以开那辆巴士。

154
00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.330
Michael is the annoying touriSt.
迈克尔是那个烦人的游客。

155
00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:21.710
Oh, for sure.
哦，当然。

156
00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:22.130
Right?
对吧？

157
00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:22.490
Yeah.
是啊。

158
