485
00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:21.470
I mean, uh-oh is right.
我的意思是，确实是“噢哦”。

486
00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:26.030
But don't worry, the SWAT team is arriving, and oh, do they arrive.
但别担心，特警队到了，而且他们出场的方式真是……绝了。

487
00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.610
We see a car fly through the air and, like, land.
我们看到一辆车飞过空中，然后，落地了。

488
00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:30.770
Unnecessarily.
完全没必要。

489
00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:31.430
Unnecessarily.
完全没必要。

490
00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:35.610
The director said he wanted this establishing shot of action.
导演说他想要这个动作戏的定场镜头。

491
00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.610
Normally, with your lead, you establish just the lead, right?
通常情况下，主角出场时，你只需要展示主角就行了，对吧？

492
00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.310
You just push in on your lead actor.
你只需要推镜头给到主角演员。

493
00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:45.470
But he wanted the car jumping to be like, this movie's about action.
但他想要那种飞车跳跃的镜头，好让观众觉得这部电影主打动作。

494
00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:48.170
And Keanu Reeves is going to get out of the driver's seat.
基努·里维斯会从驾驶座走出来。

495
00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:50.150
Jeff Daniels gets out of the passenger seat.
杰夫·丹尼尔斯从副驾驶座走出来。

496
00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.370
They go to the trunk.
他们走向后备箱。

497
00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:53.850
They start putting on all their SWAT gear.
他们开始穿上所有的特警装备。

498
00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:54.230
Yeah.
是啊。

499
00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.890
Keanu, in an interview, said it was really cool to wear all that gear.
基努在一次采访中说，穿上那些装备真的很酷。

500
00:19:58.390 --> 00:19:59.690
Well, I looked it up.
嗯，我查过了。

501
00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.990
I was like, how much does that gear weigh?
我当时就在想，那套装备到底有多重？

502
00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:06.830
Because they're about to run up, like, a gazillion flights of stairs in that gear, so I had to know.
因为他们穿着那套装备要跑上，大概，几百层楼梯，所以我必须得知道。

503
00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:14.690
So it weighs 16 pounds, like military-grade hard plate vests weigh 16 pounds.
结果是16磅，就像军用级的硬质防弹背心那样，重达16磅。

504
00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:15.950
That's a lot.
那可真够重的。

505
00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.010
It really is.
确实如此。

506
00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:17.670
Yeah.
没错。

507
00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:24.630
Jan said he really wanted the main characters and the background performers for the SWAT team to be as authentic as possible.
简说他非常希望特警队的主演和背景演员看起来尽可能真实。

508
00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:29.170
He actually had squad officers on set at all times to consult with.
他甚至在片场全程安排了特警队员进行指导。

509
00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:36.550
He said once they put the gear on, even how you walk changes, and the earpiece and how they talk to one another.
他说一旦穿上那套装备，连走路的姿势都会变，还有耳机的使用方式，以及他们彼此交谈的方式。

510
00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:37.450
Amazing.
太厉害了。

511
00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:47.390
Well, Captain Mac, who, as we said, was played by Joe Morton, who is a Tony-nominated actor and who is just fantastic, he's going to give us the lowdown on what's happening.
那么，麦克队长，正如我们所说，由乔·莫顿饰演，他是一位获得过托尼奖提名的演员，表现非常出色，他将为我们介绍目前的情况。

512
00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:50.930
There is an elevator with 13 passengers.
电梯里有13名乘客。

513
00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.830
It is rigged with explosives.
电梯被安装了炸药。

514
00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:59.770
They are hostages because the person who set the bomb is demanding $3 million as a payout.
他们成了人质，因为安放炸弹的人索要300万美元的赎金。

515
00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:05.670
They gave him an hour to get this done, but the clock has already been ticking, and now they only have 23 minutes left.
他们给了他一小时来完成这件事，但时间已经在流逝，现在只剩下23分钟了。

516
00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:10.110
So Jack is going to volunteer Harry to go inspect the bomb.
所以杰克打算让哈里主动去检查炸弹。

517
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.010
He is.
没错。

518
00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:16.550
You know, Jan talked about a writer's trick that they do in movies called Set the Clock.
你知道，简提到过电影里的一种编剧技巧，叫做“设定时钟”。

519
00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:23.570
And throughout this movie, there'll be a clock ticking, whether it's 23 minutes, or they only have 10 minutes, or they only have six minutes of fuel.
整部电影里都会有一个倒计时，不管是23分钟，还是只剩10分钟，又或者是只剩下6分钟的燃料。

520
00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:25.670
There's always the reminder of the clock.
时钟的提醒无处不在。

521
00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:29.770
I mean, also, just the speedometer is a kind of ticking clock in this movie, too.
我的意思是，速度表在这部电影里其实也是一种倒计时。

522
00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:32.570
This is why I think I haven't been able to sleep.
这就是为什么我觉得我一直睡不着觉。

523
00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:33.010
I know.
我懂。

524
00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:36.250
Because I've been under the ticking clock of this movie for so long.
因为我在这部电影的倒计时压力下待了太久了。

525
00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:42.210
Well, Harry and Jack are going to climb into the elevator shaft, and they're going to find the explosives on the top of the car.
好了，哈里和杰克要爬进电梯井，他们会在轿厢顶部发现炸药。

526
00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:43.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

527
00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:46.370
They're going to start trying to figure out what to do here.
他们开始设法解决这个问题。

528
00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:48.410
They do their first pop quiz.
他们要进行第一次突击测验了。

529
00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:49.590
Oh.
哦。

530
00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:50.390
Do you want to do it?
你想来吗？

531
00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:51.490
I printed it out, Ange.
我把它打印出来了，安吉。

532
00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:52.190
Do I?
我来吗？

533
00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:52.590
All right.
好吧。

534
00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:54.130
Do I want to do the pop quiz?
我想做这个突击测验吗？

535
00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:56.210
This is like my favorite runner of the movie.
这简直是我在这部电影里最喜欢的梗。

536
00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:56.630
All right.
好吧。

537
00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.290
I'll be Harry.
我演哈里。

538
00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:58.030
You be Jack.
你演杰克。

539
00:21:58.390 --> 00:21:58.530
Ready?
准备好了吗？

540
00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.890
Oh, I get to be Keanu?
哦，我可以演基努吗？

541
00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.030
You can be Keanu.
你可以演基努。

542
00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:01.350
Okay.
好的。

543
00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:01.610
Okay.
好的。

544
00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:02.990
All right.
好吧。

545
00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:03.670
Pop quiz.
突击测验。

546
00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:04.790
The airport.
机场。

547
00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:06.570
Gunman with one hostage.
一名持枪歹徒挟持了一名人质。

548
00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:08.230
He's using her for cover.
他正用她做掩护。

549
00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.670
He's almost to a plane.
他快要走到飞机旁了。

550
00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:11.310
You're 100 feet away.
你距离他100英尺。

551
00:22:12.110 --> 00:22:12.990
Shoot the hostage.
干掉人质。

552
00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:13.770
What?
什么？

553
00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:15.830
Take her out of the equation.
把她从这个局面中剔除掉。

554
00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:18.410
Go for the good wound, and he can't get to the plane with her.
打伤腿就行，这样他就没法带着她上飞机了。

555
00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:19.190
Clear shot.
射击角度清晰。

556
00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:20.590
You're deeply nuts.
你真是疯得彻底。

557
00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:21.150
You know that?
你知道吗？

558
00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:26.130
Lady, after this movie came out, my friends and I would say pop quiz a**hole all the time
女士，这部电影上映后，我和朋友们总是会互相说“突击测验，混蛋”。

559
00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:26.730
to each other.
对彼此说。

560
00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:28.450
Of course.
当然。

561
00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:31.110
Like, just like running errands, like going to the grocery store.
就像办点琐事，比如去杂货店买东西的时候。

562
00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:32.250
Pop quiz a**hole.
“突击测验，混蛋”。

563
00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:35.150
Do you want to grill hot dogs tonight or hamburgers?
今晚你想烤热狗还是汉堡？

564
00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:39.570
I feel like it's one of the more, like, quotable moments from the movie.
我觉得这是电影里最让人津津乐道的桥段之一。

565
00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:40.290
For sure.
确实。

566
00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:43.830
Jack is going to figure out how to diffuse the situation.
杰克会想办法化解这个局面。

567
00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:45.810
How to take the hostages out of the equation.
想办法把人质从这个局面中解救出来。

568
00:22:46.030 --> 00:22:46.370
Yes.
没错。

569
00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:46.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

570
00:22:47.110 --> 00:22:49.470
There's this giant, what do you call that thing?
有个巨大的，那个东西叫什么来着？

571
00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:50.090
A crane?
起重机？

572
00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:52.210
A crane on top of the building.
大楼顶上的起重机。

573
00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:52.550
Yeah.
对。

574
00:22:52.550 --> 00:22:53.770
And he's like, let's get a cable.
他说，我们找根缆绳。

575
00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:54.670
We're going to run up there.
我们要跑上去。

576
00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:55.590
We're going to loop this down.
我们要把它绕下来。

577
00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:56.950
We're going to attach it to the elevator.
我们要把它系在电梯上。

578
00:22:57.190 --> 00:23:03.330
Well, as you know, spoiler alert, this crane idea is going to work at first, but it's not
好吧，如你所知，剧透预警，这个起重机的主意起初是管用的，但最终

579
00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:04.550
ultimately going to hold.
支撑不住。

580
00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:05.450
We'll get there.
我们待会儿再说这个。

581
00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:05.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

582
00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:13.830
But when Jack says, how much does an elevator weigh, and he gets this idea, I looked it up.
但当杰克问电梯有多重，并想出这个主意时，我查了一下。

583
00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:15.370
How much does an elevator weigh?
电梯到底有多重？

584
00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:21.950
The average weight of an empty elevator ranges from 2,000 to 6,000 pounds.
空电梯的平均重量在2000到6000磅之间。

585
00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:22.690
That's a lot.
那可真够重的。

586
00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:23.710
That's an empty elevator.
那还是空电梯。

587
00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:25.470
We've got 13 hostages inside.
里面还有13个人质呢。

588
00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:26.710
Well.
好吧。

589
00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:29.650
By the way, the hostages are kind of freaking out.
顺便说一下，人质们当时有点崩溃了。

590
00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:30.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

591
00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:31.750
It's very tense in the elevator.
电梯里的气氛非常紧张。

592
00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:33.910
So they attach the hook.
所以他们挂上了钩子。

593
00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:35.810
Keanu Reeves is upside down.
基努·里维斯倒挂着。

594
00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:37.210
He really did that.
他是真的亲自上阵了。

595
00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:40.050
He really hung upside down on those cables, you guys.
伙计们，他是真的倒挂在那些缆绳上的。

596
00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:44.070
I almost Googled how long can you safely hang upside down, but I let it go.
我差点去谷歌搜索人倒挂多久才安全，但我还是算了。

597
00:23:44.490 --> 00:23:45.290
Well, okay.
好吧，行吧。

598
00:23:47.350 --> 00:23:49.210
Anyway, these are the things I think of.
总之，我脑子里想的就是这些。

599
00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:54.550
So our madman is going to realize that they're up to something, and he is going to blow the brakes.
所以我们的疯子意识到他们要搞鬼，于是他炸断了刹车。

600
00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:57.450
This blows out a hole in the bottom of the elevator.
这在电梯底部炸出了一个洞。

601
00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:03.650
The elevator starts plummeting all the way down to the 23rd floor when our crane finally catches.
当我们的起重机最终钩住时，电梯正一路坠向23楼。

602
00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:06.810
There is so much mayhem and panic inside this elevator.
电梯里一片混乱和恐慌。

603
00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:08.890
Have you ever been trapped inside of an elevator?
你曾经被困在电梯里吗？

604
00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:13.190
I never have, but this gives me, like, PTSD as if it happened to me.
我从来没有，但这让我感觉像是得了创伤后应激障碍，就好像发生在我身上一样。

605
00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:14.330
No, it's so scary.
不，这太可怕了。

606
00:24:14.330 --> 00:24:16.230
I have never been trapped in an elevator.
我从来没被困在电梯里过。

607
00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:23.670
But, Lady, the director shared about something that happened to him on Die Hard that inspired him for this scene.
但是，女士，导演分享了他拍摄《虎胆龙威》时发生的一件事，那件事给了他这场戏的灵感。

608
00:24:23.870 --> 00:24:24.630
You've got to hear it.
你一定要听听。

609
00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:26.490
Die Hard inspired speed.
《虎胆龙威》启发了《生死时速》。

610
00:24:26.490 --> 00:24:27.470
I love this.
我喜欢这个。

611
00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:37.470
The reason I came up to this whole elevator scene, I was going to say earlier, is that during the filming of Die Hard, I once myself got stuck in an elevator.
我之前想说，我之所以构思出整个电梯场景，是因为在拍摄《虎胆龙威》时，我自己曾被困在电梯里。

612
00:24:37.770 --> 00:24:43.190
I mean, it was actually at the building of the Fox Plaza building.
我的意思是，那实际上是在福克斯广场大厦。

613
00:24:43.190 --> 00:24:51.730
And it was really eerie we were sitting on the 40th floor, and we were there for hours, and finally the fire department came and took us out via the top.
当时真的很诡异，我们被困在40楼，待了好几个小时，最后消防部门赶到，把我们从顶部救了出来。

614
00:24:51.790 --> 00:24:55.630
And we had to climb out and jump from one elevator to the other elevator.
我们不得不爬出去，从一个电梯跳到另一个电梯。

615
00:24:55.950 --> 00:25:00.510
And that has steppersed me for a very, very long time.
那件事让我留下了很长很长时间的心理阴影。

616
00:25:01.010 --> 00:25:04.030
Because it feels so incredibly claustrophobic in there.
因为在里面感觉极其幽闭恐惧。

617
00:25:04.270 --> 00:25:07.570
You know, all those people around you, it gets hot very quickly.
你知道，周围全是人，很快就会变得很热。

618
00:25:08.070 --> 00:25:10.330
It's very hard to, you know, to stay calm.
你知道，很难保持冷静。

619
00:25:10.330 --> 00:25:13.330
I mean, if anybody would panic, it would instantly be chaotic.
我的意思是，如果有人惊慌失措，瞬间就会陷入混乱。

620
00:25:13.570 --> 00:25:16.450
This was kind of a traumatic experience.
这算是一种创伤性经历。

621
00:25:16.470 --> 00:25:24.810
And that whole feeling of claustrophobia, I thought this would be, you know, that would be, like, ideal for this type of, for this, for my movie.
那种幽闭恐惧的感觉，我觉得对于我的电影来说，是非常理想的素材。

622
00:25:24.890 --> 00:25:27.870
I wanted to make sure that people could identify with it.
我想确保观众能产生共鸣。

623
00:25:28.270 --> 00:25:29.430
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

624
00:25:29.550 --> 00:25:30.030
Yeah.
是啊。

625
00:25:30.210 --> 00:25:31.230
Can you believe that?
你能相信吗？

626
00:25:31.450 --> 00:25:37.550
He got stuck in an elevator while filming Die Hard, and then he used that experience to inform speed.
他在拍摄《虎胆龙威》时被困在电梯里，然后他利用那次经历为《生死时速》提供了灵感。

627
00:25:37.950 --> 00:25:38.290
Yeah.
没错。

628
00:25:38.290 --> 00:25:41.350
This is maybe my favorite fact ever.
这可能是我听过最喜欢的事实了。

629
00:25:41.630 --> 00:25:42.590
He's fascinating.
他太迷人了。

630
00:25:43.010 --> 00:25:51.550
I would say of all of those DVD extras, the best thing on it is Jan's commentary and also all of the behind the scenes of the stunts.
如果要说那些DVD花絮，我觉得最棒的就是简的评论音轨，还有所有关于特技的幕后制作。

631
00:25:51.870 --> 00:25:53.610
What about the Billy Idol music video?
那比利·艾多尔的音乐录影带呢？

632
00:25:53.830 --> 00:25:54.550
I would skip it.
我会跳过它。

633
00:25:58.100 --> 00:26:01.720
Well, listen, like I said, that crane is not going to hold.
好吧，听着，就像我说的，那台起重机撑不住的。

634
00:26:01.880 --> 00:26:10.820
But they are going to try to get all the passengers out of this tiny space as it continues to kind of, like, fall.
