00:38:33.710 --> 00:38:34.050
And litter.
还有垃圾。

952
00:38:34.170 --> 00:38:34.970
Times have changed.
时代变了。

953
00:38:34.990 --> 00:38:36.810
In the very first opening shot.
在最初的开场镜头里。

954
00:38:37.150 --> 00:38:37.450
Yes.
是的。

955
00:38:37.730 --> 00:38:38.890
She gets on the bus.
她上了公交车。

956
00:38:39.010 --> 00:38:45.210
She takes a seat and is immediately chatted up by a tourist, played by Alan Ruck from Ferris Bueller's Day Off.
她找了个座位坐下，立刻就有个游客过来搭讪，那个游客是由《春天不是读书天》里的艾伦·拉克饰演的。

957
00:38:45.210 --> 00:38:46.430
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

958
00:38:46.670 --> 00:38:49.370
His character didn't used to be a touriSt.
他的角色原本不是游客。

959
00:38:49.850 --> 00:38:53.270
He was a totally different character in the original script.
在最初的剧本里，他是一个完全不同的角色。

960
00:38:53.450 --> 00:38:55.990
And I found an audio clip of him talking about it.
我找到了一段他谈论这件事的音频片段。

961
00:38:56.050 --> 00:38:57.250
And I thought maybe we could hear it.
我想也许我们可以听听看。

962
00:38:59.170 --> 00:39:10.670
Actually, my character was supposed to be a really sort of loathsome, entitled attorney whose BMW was in the shop.
其实，我的角色原本应该是一个非常令人讨厌、自以为是的律师，他的宝马车送去修理了。

963
00:39:10.670 --> 00:39:13.550
And he was stuck riding the bus.
所以他不得不坐公交车。

964
00:39:14.090 --> 00:39:25.390
And then when I auditioned for it, Jan de Bont decided to go a different way with it and just turned me into this, you know, yokel, this mumbling touriSt.
后来我去试镜的时候，扬·德·邦特决定换个方向，把我变成了这样一个乡巴佬，一个嘟嘟囔囔的游客。

965
00:39:25.810 --> 00:39:26.990
And I think it worked well.
我觉得效果很好。

966
00:39:27.050 --> 00:39:29.190
I think it was actually a better choice.
我认为这其实是一个更好的选择。

967
00:39:30.350 --> 00:39:33.070
So, you know, Sandra Bullock is going to have to get away from him.
所以，你知道，桑德拉·布洛克得想办法躲开他。

968
00:39:33.070 --> 00:39:35.390
So she's going to pretend like there's gum on her seat.
于是她假装座位上有口香糖。

969
00:39:35.750 --> 00:39:36.350
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

970
00:39:36.410 --> 00:39:38.970
The whole gum bit was improvised by Sandra Bullock.
整个口香糖的桥段是桑德拉·布洛克即兴发挥的。

971
00:39:39.470 --> 00:39:39.910
Really?
真的吗？

972
00:39:39.910 --> 00:39:40.270
Yeah.
是的。

973
00:39:40.690 --> 00:39:43.390
Just in the moment, they're trying to figure out how to get her away.
就在那一刻，他们正试图想办法让她脱身。

974
00:39:43.530 --> 00:39:44.810
And so she did this gum bit.
于是她就演了这段口香糖的戏。

975
00:39:44.970 --> 00:39:45.730
I thought it worked great.
我觉得效果棒极了。

976
00:39:45.910 --> 00:39:53.110
I thought that was really smart because it was a very, like, likable, kind way for her to, like, brush this guy off.
我觉得那真的很聪明，因为这是一种非常讨人喜欢、委婉的方式，让她可以打发掉这个家伙。

977
00:39:53.550 --> 00:39:57.090
So she's going to get up and then she's going to sit down next to Beth Grant.
然后她起身坐到了贝丝·格兰特旁边。

978
00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:57.630
Helen!
海伦！

979
00:39:58.310 --> 00:40:02.230
When we talk to Beth about this, you have to listen to her interview.
当我们和贝丝谈论这件事时，你一定要听听她的采访。

980
00:40:02.430 --> 00:40:04.310
We won't rehash it right now.
我们现在就不赘述了。

981
00:40:04.470 --> 00:40:06.010
But there was, like, this whole other script.
但当时确实有另一个剧本。

982
00:40:06.010 --> 00:40:08.510
Like, the one where Alan Ruck was, like, the angry businessman.
就像那个艾伦·拉克饰演愤怒商人的版本。

983
00:40:08.510 --> 00:40:11.910
There was this whole other thing in the original script.
最初的剧本里还有完全不同的内容。

984
00:40:12.070 --> 00:40:12.910
It's so interesting.
太有趣了。

985
00:40:13.050 --> 00:40:14.050
You have to listen to her interview.
你一定要听听她的采访。

986
00:40:14.270 --> 00:40:17.370
All of her behind-the-scenes details are so wonderful.
她所有的幕后细节都太精彩了。

987
00:40:17.730 --> 00:40:22.830
So we kind of pan around the bus now and we get a sense of who all of our passengers are.
现在我们环顾一下公交车，了解一下车上的乘客都是谁。

988
00:40:23.270 --> 00:40:26.970
Jack is racing through traffic trying to catch up to the bus.
杰克正在车流中飞驰，试图追上那辆公交车。

989
00:40:28.210 --> 00:40:31.390
He's going to bang on the bus door and the window cracks.
他会猛拍公交车的门，然后玻璃就裂了。

990
00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:31.790
Yeah.
没错。

991
00:40:31.970 --> 00:40:32.750
That was not planned.
那不是计划好的。

992
00:40:33.530 --> 00:40:33.890
What?
什么？

993
00:40:34.210 --> 00:40:34.310
Yeah.
是的。

994
00:40:34.450 --> 00:40:35.130
That just happened.
那是意外发生的。

995
00:40:35.590 --> 00:40:39.190
And then it kind of became a continuity thing because sometimes you see a bus with a door that's cracked.
后来这成了一个连贯性问题，因为有时候你会看到公交车门是裂开的。

996
00:40:39.350 --> 00:40:40.510
Sometimes it doesn't have a crack.
有时候又没有裂痕。

997
00:40:40.870 --> 00:40:41.850
Crack, no crack, crack.
有裂痕，没裂痕，有裂痕。

998
00:40:42.090 --> 00:40:42.650
Crack, no crack.
有裂痕，没裂痕。

999
00:40:43.170 --> 00:40:43.530
Wow.
哇。

1000
00:40:44.230 --> 00:40:50.950
Well, as the bus is driving away, leaving Jack on the side of the road, the bus is not yet going 50 miles an hour.
当公交车开走，把杰克留在路边时，车速还没达到每小时50英里。

1001
00:40:51.170 --> 00:40:53.370
So the bomb has not been engaged.
所以炸弹还没有被触发。

1002
00:40:53.690 --> 00:40:53.970
Uh-uh.
嗯。

1003
00:40:54.150 --> 00:40:57.290
And this sort of creates a big plot hole.
这在某种程度上造成了一个巨大的剧情漏洞。

1004
00:40:57.470 --> 00:41:02.670
In an otherwise pretty tight script, it was pointed out in Janet Maslin's review.
在原本相当严谨的剧本中，珍妮特·马斯林的影评指出了这一点。

1005
00:41:02.670 --> 00:41:03.230
Yes, Janet!
没错，珍妮特！

1006
00:41:03.790 --> 00:41:04.890
Do you know Janet?
你认识珍妮特吗？

1007
00:41:04.890 --> 00:41:08.010
I mean, I don't know her, but her review's amazing.
我是说，我不认识她，但她的影评写得太棒了。

1008
00:41:08.270 --> 00:41:10.370
Yes, her New York Times review.
是的，她在《纽约时报》上的那篇影评。

1009
00:41:10.850 --> 00:41:15.590
She said, at this point, the bus is only going about 15 or 20 miles an hour.
她说，在这一刻，巴士的时速只有15到20英里左右。

1010
00:41:15.850 --> 00:41:17.130
He has a gun.
他有枪。

1011
00:41:17.350 --> 00:41:21.750
Why doesn't he shoot out the tires so that the bomb is never engaged?
为什么他不直接打爆轮胎，这样炸弹就不会被触发了？

1012
00:41:22.310 --> 00:41:33.510
Well, this review has haunted screenwriter Graham Yost, who 20 years later was still discussing this and said, yes, he wished he had thought of this.
嗯，这篇影评一直困扰着编剧格雷厄姆·约斯特，二十年后他还在讨论这件事，并说他真希望自己当时想到了这一点。

1013
00:41:33.510 --> 00:41:44.290
He said, if he had to do it all over again, he would have Jack pull out his gun, and then he would have the driver of the Jaguar purposely bump Jack,
他说，如果一切能重来，他会让杰克掏出枪，然后让那辆捷豹的司机故意撞向杰克，

1014
00:41:44.890 --> 00:41:53.090
thinking that Jack was like a bad guy, and then Jack's gun would go flying, and then Jack would get in the guy's car.
以为杰克是个坏人，接着杰克的枪就会飞出去，然后杰克就能坐进那个人的车里。

1015
00:41:53.450 --> 00:41:56.610
And that that would be like a perfect way to solve this problem.
他说那将是解决这个问题的完美方式。

1016
00:41:57.090 --> 00:41:57.270
Right.
没错。

1017
00:41:57.510 --> 00:42:02.290
Of course, then Jack wouldn't have had a gun to pull on the passenger who pulls a gun on him.
当然，那样的话，杰克就没有枪去对付那个对他掏枪的乘客了。

1018
00:42:02.450 --> 00:42:03.350
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1019
00:42:03.350 --> 00:42:04.730
Then he wouldn't have had a stalemate.
那样他就没法形成僵持局面了。

1020
00:42:04.930 --> 00:42:10.190
I don't know how to tell Graham that, because he was really excited to have fixed this plot hole.
我不知道该怎么告诉格雷厄姆，因为他当时真的很兴奋自己填补了这个剧情漏洞。

1021
00:42:10.250 --> 00:42:11.810
Well, Graham, I think he needed his gun.
嗯，格雷厄姆，我觉得他当时确实需要那把枪。

1022
00:42:12.070 --> 00:42:15.790
Otherwise, the passenger with the gun would have had the bus pulled over.
否则，那个持枪的乘客早就让巴士停下来了。

1023
00:42:16.210 --> 00:42:17.690
This is a really good point.
这确实是个很好的观点。

1024
00:42:18.070 --> 00:42:18.810
Just saying.
我只是随口一说。

1025
00:42:19.070 --> 00:42:19.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1026
00:42:19.630 --> 00:42:25.390
Well, Jack is now going to flag down a guy driving a Jaguar license plate toon man.
好了，杰克现在要拦下一辆车牌号是“卡通人”的捷豹车。

1027
00:42:25.610 --> 00:42:25.990
Yes.
是的。

1028
00:42:25.990 --> 00:42:27.630
He was played by Glenn Plummer.
那个角色由格伦·普卢默饰演。

1029
00:42:28.050 --> 00:42:29.910
He also comes back for Speed 2.
他后来还出演了《生死时速2》。

1030
00:42:30.550 --> 00:42:31.070
Really?
真的吗？

1031
00:42:31.070 --> 00:42:32.210
Yes, he plays Maurice.
是的，他饰演莫里斯。

1032
00:42:33.090 --> 00:42:33.390
Wow.
哇。

1033
00:42:33.690 --> 00:42:33.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1034
00:42:34.470 --> 00:42:37.810
Jack is going to say, listen, I need, you know, basically he needs to use his car.
杰克要说，听着，我需要，你知道，基本上他需要用他的车。

1035
00:42:38.170 --> 00:42:38.610
Yeah.
是的。

1036
00:42:38.950 --> 00:42:39.390
Get over.
靠边。

1037
00:42:39.530 --> 00:42:40.050
I'm driving.
我来开。

1038
00:42:40.310 --> 00:42:40.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1039
00:42:40.930 --> 00:42:44.830
He's going to catch up with the bus right as it hits 50 miles an hour.
他刚好在巴士时速达到50英里时追上了它。

1040
00:42:45.070 --> 00:42:46.010
The worst luck.
真是倒霉透顶。

1041
00:42:46.170 --> 00:42:46.870
The worst luck.
倒霉透顶。

1042
00:42:46.870 --> 00:42:48.490
Jack, the bomb is activated.
杰克，炸弹启动了。

1043
00:42:49.090 --> 00:42:53.090
And now Jack has to somehow tell Sam he's got to keep it at 50.
现在杰克必须想办法告诉山姆，他必须保持时速在50英里以上。

1044
00:42:53.550 --> 00:42:53.790
Yes.
是的。

1045
00:42:54.090 --> 00:42:58.770
They managed to communicate all this with, I guess, writing it on a piece of paper and
他们设法沟通了这一切，我想，是通过写在纸条上，

1046
00:42:58.770 --> 00:43:00.490
then screaming it in through the door.
然后对着车门大喊。

1047
00:43:00.490 --> 00:43:03.450
But Keanu now, he needs to get on the bus.
但基努现在需要上那辆巴士。

1048
00:43:03.730 --> 00:43:04.210
Okay?
好吗？

1049
00:43:04.470 --> 00:43:05.310
He has to get on.
他必须上去。

1050
00:43:05.830 --> 00:43:09.930
This stunt of him getting on the bus, Keanu did this himself.
这个他跳上巴士的特技，是基努亲自完成的。

1051
00:43:09.930 --> 00:43:12.710
He really jumped from a car onto a bus.
他真的从一辆车跳上了一辆巴士。

1052
00:43:12.870 --> 00:43:14.790
They were going 50 miles an hour.
当时车速是每小时50英里。

1053
00:43:14.950 --> 00:43:17.250
The two vehicles had to stay the same speed.
两辆车必须保持相同的速度。

1054
00:43:17.670 --> 00:43:21.150
The director didn't want him to do it, but Keanu trained with the stunt team.
导演本不想让他亲自上阵，但基努还是和特技团队一起进行了训练。

1055
00:43:21.510 --> 00:43:22.470
And he did.
而且他真的做到了。

1056
00:43:22.770 --> 00:43:24.490
He did the dang thing.
他真的完成了那件事。

1057
00:43:24.990 --> 00:43:29.930
Here is the stunt coordinator, Gary Himes, discussing doing this stunt with Keanu.
这位是特技协调员加里·海姆斯，他在谈论与基努一起完成这个特技动作。

1058
00:43:30.850 --> 00:43:36.450
One of the situations that comes to mind early on was when he's transferring from the Jaguar
我最先想到的情况之一，就是他从捷豹车上转移到

1059
00:43:36.450 --> 00:43:37.150
to the bus.
巴士上的那一幕。

1060
00:43:37.270 --> 00:43:38.530
We had talked about it.
我们之前讨论过这件事。

1061
00:43:38.650 --> 00:43:39.450
We had talked it through.
我们详细商量过。

1062
00:43:39.610 --> 00:43:41.010
He seemed very comfortable with it.
他看起来对此非常有把握。

1063
00:43:41.730 --> 00:43:46.970
I went ahead and built a platform under the bus so, indeed, if he did miss, he wasn't going
我特意在巴士下面搭建了一个平台，这样一来，如果他真的失手了，也不会

1064
00:43:46.970 --> 00:43:49.590
to hit the ground because we're running 50 miles an hour down the freeway.
直接摔在地上，因为当时我们正以每小时50英里的速度在高速公路上行驶。

1065
00:43:49.590 --> 00:43:57.090
And once we got out there and the first time we went to shoot it, he was just a little
当我们到了现场，第一次准备拍摄时，他还是稍微

1066
00:43:57.090 --> 00:43:59.630
bit uncomfortable with the situation.
感到有些不安。

1067
00:43:59.690 --> 00:44:02.350
So I cut the shot and we went back.
所以我喊了停，我们退了回去。

1068
00:44:02.510 --> 00:44:05.990
We talked about making a couple little changes, nothing major.
我们商量着做了一些小改动，没什么大不了的。

1069
00:44:06.390 --> 00:44:08.170
And he did it.
然后他就做到了。

1070
00:44:08.210 --> 00:44:12.690
And he did it so well that we wanted to get one more take of that.
而且他完成得非常出色，以至于我们想再拍一条。

1071
00:44:12.690 --> 00:44:15.910
And we actually moved the car and the bus further apart.
我们实际上把轿车和巴士之间的距离拉得更开了。

1072
00:44:16.190 --> 00:44:17.830
And he went for it.
但他还是跳了过去。

1073
00:44:17.910 --> 00:44:19.630
And I mean, it was a great shot.
我是说，那真是一个很棒的镜头。

1074
00:44:20.250 --> 00:44:23.830
Well, I have a second The Office Speed crossover for you.
好吧，我还有第二个关于《办公室》和《生死时速》的联动点要告诉你。

1075
00:44:24.010 --> 00:44:25.510
You mean besides Beth Grant?
你是说除了贝丝·格兰特之外？

1076
00:44:25.830 --> 00:44:26.330
Yes.
没错。

1077
00:44:26.850 --> 00:44:31.550
Gary Himes worked on The Hangover Part 3 with Ed HelMs.
加里·海姆斯曾与艾德·赫尔姆斯合作过《宿醉3》。

1078
00:44:31.830 --> 00:44:33.150
Well, there you go.
好吧，原来如此。

1079
00:44:33.890 --> 00:44:39.930
I want you to know at 39 minutes and 55 seconds, as Keanu is getting ready to jump onto the
我想让你知道，在39分55秒的时候，当基努准备跳上

1080
00:44:39.930 --> 00:44:44.750
bus, there's a shot from behind and the wind, you can tell how fast they're going because
巴士时，有一个从背后拍摄的镜头，你可以看出风很大，因为他们开得很快，

1081
00:44:44.750 --> 00:44:49.350
the wind whips up the back of his shirt and you can see his mic pack.
风吹起了他的衬衫后摆，你可以看到他的麦克风发射器。

1082
00:44:49.630 --> 00:44:54.250
Well, I think we should take a break because when we come back, Jack is on the bus, y'all.
好吧，我觉得我们该休息一下了，因为回来之后，杰克就要上巴士了，各位。

1083
00:44:54.750 --> 00:44:56.570
He's on the bus and a lot happens.
他上了巴士，然后发生了很多事。

1084
00:45:05.580 --> 00:45:06.340
We're back.
我们回来了。

1085
00:45:06.580 --> 00:45:07.760
We're on the bus, you guys.
伙计们，我们现在在巴士上了。

1086
00:45:07.760 --> 00:45:12.300
Jack is on the bus and right away, there's even more mayhem.
杰克上了巴士，紧接着，更多的混乱随之而来。

1087
00:45:12.920 --> 00:45:13.280
Yes.
没错。

1088
00:45:13.540 --> 00:45:19.000
A man pulls a gun on Jack because he thinks that Jack has boarded the bus for him.
有个男人用枪指着杰克，因为他以为杰克上车是为了抓他。

1089
00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:19.380
To get him.
为了对付他。

1090
00:45:19.740 --> 00:45:19.840
Yeah.
是的。

1091
00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:22.140
The man was played by Daniel Villarreal.
那个男人由丹尼尔·比利亚雷亚尔饰演。

1092
00:45:22.500 --> 00:45:25.620
And yeah, Jack is like, I'm not here for you.
没错，杰克当时的意思是，我不是冲你来的。

1093
00:45:26.300 --> 00:45:27.760
He has some great dialogue.
他有几句很棒的台词。

1094
00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.200
He's like, we're good.
他说，我们没事。

1095
00:45:29.600 --> 00:45:30.380
We're good.
我们没问题。

1096
00:45:30.380 --> 00:45:31.840
And he's going to put his gun away.
然后他就要把枪收起来了。

1097
00:45:32.060 --> 00:45:34.880
His gun that he needed to have for the standoff.
他本来在对峙中需要用到的那把枪。

1098
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:35.460
Just saying.
我只是随口一提。

1099
00:45:35.640 --> 00:45:36.560
No, this is true.
不，这是真的。

1100
00:45:36.560 --> 00:45:38.260
He's going to use his gun later, too.
他后来还要用到那把枪呢。

1101
00:45:38.480 --> 00:45:41.220
But one of the other passengers on the bus is going to see an opportunity.
但车上的另一名乘客看到了机会。

1102
00:45:41.260 --> 00:45:43.480
He's going to tackle the guy with the gun.
他打算扑向那个拿枪的人。

1103
00:45:43.480 --> 00:45:44.660
The gun's going to go off.
枪会走火。

1104
00:45:44.720 --> 00:45:46.680
It's going to shoot the bus driver, Sam.
子弹会击中公交车司机萨姆。

1105
00:45:47.040 --> 00:45:47.480
Yes.
没错。

1106
00:45:47.740 --> 00:45:48.580
In the shoulder.
击中肩膀。

1107
00:45:48.840 --> 00:45:54.640
Now he like falls over the steering wheel and all of a sudden, Annie's got to step in to drive.
他会倒在方向盘上，安妮不得不接手开车。

1108
00:45:55.160 --> 00:45:55.440
Yes.
是的。

1109
00:45:55.900 --> 00:46:00.200
This is when Jack is going to tell everyone the news that there's a bomb on the bus because
这时杰克会告诉大家车上有炸弹，因为

1110
00:46:00.200 --> 00:46:01.640
Annie's starting to slow down.
安妮开始减速了。

1111
00:46:01.820 --> 00:46:03.360
Obviously, she needs to slow down.
显然，她需要减速。

1112
00:46:03.520 --> 00:46:04.500
Sam has been shot.
萨姆中枪了。

1113
00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:04.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1114
00:46:04.860 --> 00:46:09.020
And he's like, no, no, there's a bomb on this bus.
而他却说，不，不，这辆车上有炸弹。

1115
00:46:09.840 --> 00:46:10.700
Everyone's like, what?
大家都惊呆了，什么？

1116
00:46:11.280 --> 00:46:12.220
My gosh.
天哪。

1117
00:46:12.380 --> 00:46:12.540
What?
什么？

1118
00:46:12.880 --> 00:46:18.460
So I wanted to say that in the first version of the script, the character of Annie was a paramedic.
我想说的是，在剧本的初稿中，安妮这个角色是一名护理人员。

1119
00:46:18.760 --> 00:46:23.340
And this was to justify the fact that she could drive a bus really quickly through traffic.
这样设定是为了解释她为什么能开着公交车在车流中飞驰。

1120
00:46:23.340 --> 00:46:29.920
Then in the second iteration, like you said, she became this comedic driver's ed teacher.
后来在第二版剧本里，正如你所说，她变成了一名滑稽的驾校教练。

1121
00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:36.060
Finally, they settled with just that she had her license revoked for speeding.
最后，他们定稿为她是因为超速被吊销了驾照。

1122
00:46:36.060 --> 00:46:40.500
Well, in deleted scenes, there was more that she shares with Helen.
其实在删减片段里，她和海伦还有更多交流。

1123
00:46:41.120 --> 00:46:41.380
Really?
真的吗？

1124
00:46:41.680 --> 00:46:41.840
Yeah.
是的。

1125
00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:46.580
She tells Helen she's a graphic designer, but currently working at like a fast food restaurant.
她告诉海伦她是平面设计师，但目前在一家快餐店打工。

1126
00:46:46.880 --> 00:46:47.320
Oh.
哦。

1127
00:46:47.620 --> 00:46:47.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1128
00:46:48.220 --> 00:46:52.760
Well, I'll have you know, Sandra Bullock trained to actually be able to drive a bus.
我得告诉你，桑德拉·布洛克为了这部戏专门去学了开公交车。

1129
00:46:52.760 --> 00:46:57.240
And she passed a bus driving test before the movie started shooting.
在电影开拍前，她还通过了公交车驾驶考试。

1130
00:46:57.440 --> 00:46:59.560
However, she is never driving the bus.
然而，她其实从来没真正开过那辆车。

1131
00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:00.200
Not one time.
一次都没有。

1132
00:47:00.200 --> 00:47:01.420
She's not really driving the bus.
她并不是真的在开车。

1133
00:47:01.660 --> 00:47:06.460
In the commentary, they did say when they were at the airport and they had all that big open space,
在评论音轨里，他们确实提到过，当他们在机场有那么大一片空地时，

1134
00:47:06.940 --> 00:47:09.500
they let her drive just, you know, one or two.
他们让她开了一两次。

1135
00:47:09.680 --> 00:47:09.730
For a second.
就一会儿。

1136
00:47:09.730 --> 00:47:12.020
Yeah, and she did hit a few cones.
是啊，而且她还撞倒了几个路标桶。

1137
00:47:12.280 --> 00:47:12.880
Oh, dear.
天哪。

1138
00:47:13.100 --> 00:47:13.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1139
00:47:13.760 --> 00:47:17.680
Well, the person who was actually driving the bus was stunt driver Gil Combs,
其实真正开车的人是特技车手吉尔·库姆斯，

1140
00:47:17.700 --> 00:47:20.760
and he was hidden all over this bus.
他藏在车上的各个角落。

1141
00:47:21.280 --> 00:47:24.660
A lot of the time, he was on top of the bus.
很多时候，他都在车顶上。

1142
00:47:24.740 --> 00:47:24.880
Yeah.
没错。

1143
00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:26.680
They built like this rig.
他们搭建了一个装置。

1144
00:47:26.900 --> 00:47:28.780
Or like a cage that he sat in.
或者说是一个他坐在里面的笼子。

1145
00:47:28.980 --> 00:47:30.700
I mean, cage-ish.
我是说，勉强算个笼子吧。

1146
00:47:31.140 --> 00:47:31.620
Generous.
这词用得真大方。

1147
00:47:32.040 --> 00:47:33.580
There were a couple of bars.
其实就是几根杆子。

1148
00:47:34.100 --> 00:47:38.380
And you can see him up there with an operating pedal and a big steering wheel.
你可以看到他在上面操作踏板和一个大方向盘。

1149
00:47:38.480 --> 00:47:38.940
And a helmet.
还戴着头盔。

1150
00:47:39.700 --> 00:47:41.080
A helmet, but shorts.
戴着头盔，但穿着短裤。

1151
00:47:41.300 --> 00:47:41.580
I know.
我知道。

1152
00:47:41.820 --> 00:47:46.700
I just, I was looking at him and I was like, I mean, what, you're, if you fall off the top of that bus,
我只是，我当时看着他，心想，我是说，如果，如果你从那辆巴士顶上掉下来，

1153
00:47:46.840 --> 00:47:48.980
the skin on your legs is going to be shredded.
你腿上的皮会被磨烂的。

1154
00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:50.100
Well, it was September.
嗯，那是九月。

1155
00:47:50.380 --> 00:47:51.360
He made a choice.
他做出了选择。

1156
00:47:51.520 --> 00:47:52.380
I guess so.
我想也是。

1157
00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:54.820
They also put him at the back of the bus.
他们还把他安排在巴士后面。

1158
00:47:54.940 --> 00:47:57.540
They put him low in one of the seats sometimes.
有时他们让他坐在靠下的座位上。

1159
00:47:57.680 --> 00:48:01.940
He was like sitting basically on the floor, and they said they had to give him a little tiny mini wheel.
他几乎是坐在地板上，他们说必须给他一个小小的迷你方向盘。

1160
00:48:02.800 --> 00:48:05.980
They put him all over the place to hide him depending on the camera angle.
他们根据摄像机角度把他安排在各处以隐藏他。

1161
00:48:06.440 --> 00:48:08.520
Well, Jack is going to get on the phone with Harry,
好吧，杰克要和哈里通电话，

1162
00:48:08.520 --> 00:48:11.380
and they decide he should check out this bomb.
他们决定他应该去检查一下那个炸弹。

1163
00:48:11.740 --> 00:48:16.820
Can he get somehow like eyes on this bomb?
他能想办法亲眼看看那个炸弹吗？

1164
00:48:16.960 --> 00:48:17.160
Right.
没错。

1165
00:48:17.540 --> 00:48:17.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1166
00:48:18.100 --> 00:48:21.040
So they're going to remember that there's like this access panel,
所以他们会记得有这样一个检修口，

1167
00:48:21.280 --> 00:48:24.200
and he's going to stick his head down, and he's going to look at this bomb.
他会把头伸下去，去看看那个炸弹。

1168
00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:28.160
This is when I said it really would have been nice if someone had an iPhone.
这就是我说的，如果当时有人有部iPhone就好了。

1169
00:48:28.440 --> 00:48:29.340
I thought so, too.
我也这么想。

1170
00:48:29.440 --> 00:48:34.160
He's playing this game of telephone with the tourist and Harry and him,
他在和游客、哈里还有他自己玩这种传话游戏，

1171
00:48:34.300 --> 00:48:39.640
but instead he could have just like put it on a FaceTime and been like, Harry, this is what it looks like.
但其实他本可以直接打个FaceTime说，哈里，这就是它现在的样子。

1172
00:48:39.740 --> 00:48:39.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1173
00:48:39.790 --> 00:48:40.440
What are your thoughts?
你有什么想法？

1174
00:48:40.700 --> 00:48:41.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1175
00:48:41.600 --> 00:48:44.480
Well, while all of this is going on, the bus is slowing down.
好吧，在这一切发生的同时，巴士正在减速。

1176
00:48:44.620 --> 00:48:45.220
There's some traffic.
前面有些交通拥堵。

1177
00:48:45.440 --> 00:48:47.180
Annie is trying to get Jack's attention.
安妮正试图引起杰克的注意。

1178
00:48:47.180 --> 00:48:48.120
She's like, hello, hello.
她在那喊，喂，喂。

1179
00:48:48.400 --> 00:48:52.980
She grabs a little microphone thing and screams, hey, officer.
她抓起一个小麦克风大喊，嘿，警官。

1180
00:48:53.520 --> 00:48:54.520
On or off.
开还是关。

1181
00:48:54.640 --> 00:48:55.320
On or off.
开还是关。

1182
00:48:55.460 --> 00:48:57.960
That was Sandra Bullock's idea, grabbing that little microphone.
那是桑德拉·布洛克的主意，抓起那个小麦克风。

1183
00:48:58.280 --> 00:48:59.520
I really liked that.
我真的很喜欢那个设计。

1184
00:48:59.620 --> 00:49:00.220
I know.
我知道。

1185
00:49:00.880 --> 00:49:02.620
Jack says, get off the freeway.
杰克说，离开高速公路。

1186
00:49:02.820 --> 00:49:03.180
Off.
离开。

1187
00:49:03.380 --> 00:49:06.820
She's going to run into a series of pretty much anything.
她会撞上一连串几乎任何东西。

1188
00:49:07.000 --> 00:49:07.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1189
00:49:08.720 --> 00:49:10.180
Cones, water barrels.
锥形路标，水桶。

1190
00:49:10.180 --> 00:49:14.280
Beth talked about this with us, so you guys be sure and listen to her interview.
贝丝和我们聊过这个，所以你们一定要去听听她的采访。

1191
00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:18.380
And then she's going to run into a baby carriage.
然后她会撞向一辆婴儿车。

1192
00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:19.100
Oh, God.
天哪。

1193
00:49:19.100 --> 00:49:20.560
A woman crossing the street.
一个正在过马路的女人。

1194
00:49:20.760 --> 00:49:21.000
Okay.
好吧。

1195
00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:25.560
I guess one of the things they felt like when they tested the movie that really sold this moment
我想他们在测试这部电影时觉得真正让这一刻变得可信的一点是，

1196
00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:28.020
is that it's not one woman with a carriage.
那不是一个带着婴儿车的女人。

1197
00:49:28.300 --> 00:49:29.660
It's two women talking.
是两个正在交谈的女人。

1198
00:49:29.660 --> 00:49:33.060
So you're thinking maybe there's a baby in that baby carriage.
所以你会觉得那辆婴儿车里可能有个婴儿。

1199
00:49:33.540 --> 00:49:33.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1200
00:49:34.140 --> 00:49:37.760
This was a note from Fox during the development period.
这是福克斯在开发期间提出的意见。

1201
00:49:37.760 --> 00:49:42.760
The writer said the note was like, what if they like almost hit a baby carriage or something?
编剧说那张纸条的内容大概是，如果他们差点撞到婴儿车之类的会怎么样？

1202
00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:44.540
That would really up the tension here.
那确实会增加这里的紧张感。

1203
00:49:45.160 --> 00:49:47.400
And the writer was kind of like, you know what?
编剧当时就想，你知道吗？

1204
00:49:47.740 --> 00:49:52.500
It feels like a cheat, you know, like in movies when there's a car chase and then the car runs
这感觉像是在作弊，你知道，就像电影里的追车戏，然后车子撞进

1205
00:49:52.500 --> 00:49:56.460
through a fruit stand, like something just like not at all dangerous.
水果摊一样，那种根本一点都不危险的东西。

1206
00:49:57.120 --> 00:50:02.820
So he said he remembered that he saw a guy in New York City walking across the street with a
所以他说他记得在纽约看到一个人推着一辆

1207
00:50:02.820 --> 00:50:04.340
shopping cart full of cans.
装满罐头的购物车过马路。

1208
00:50:04.340 --> 00:50:08.580
He's like, what if there were cans in the baby carriage?
他说，如果婴儿车里装的是罐头会怎样？

1209
00:50:09.280 --> 00:50:13.840
And then it was Jan's idea to use like one of those really classic English praMs.
后来是简提议用那种非常经典的英式婴儿车。

1210
00:50:14.520 --> 00:50:17.720
Well, I felt like Sandra Bullock's reaction was like what I would have done.
嗯，我觉得桑德拉·布洛克的反应和我当时会做的一样。

1211
00:50:17.840 --> 00:50:18.980
I'd be like, oh, my God, oh, my God, baby.
我会说，天哪，天哪，宝宝。

1212
00:50:19.380 --> 00:50:19.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1213
00:50:19.800 --> 00:50:22.720
I will say I felt like Jack got over it very quickly.
我得说我觉得杰克从这件事里恢复得太快了。

1214
00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:27.620
I feel like Jack was like, like they hit the baby stroller.
我觉得杰克当时就像是，他们撞到了婴儿车。

1215
00:50:27.900 --> 00:50:29.480
And then he's like, oh, no, we're good.
然后他就说，哦，没事，我们很好。

1216
00:50:29.860 --> 00:50:30.560
I'm like, what?
我就想，什么？

1217
00:50:30.700 --> 00:50:31.520
That was so quick.
这也太快了。

1218
00:50:31.740 --> 00:50:32.000
Why?
为什么？

1219
00:50:34.470 --> 00:50:36.110
Well, this isn't the only drama.
嗯，这还不是唯一的戏剧性事件。

1220
00:50:36.730 --> 00:50:42.730
There's going to be a really ugly right turn coming up in order to get back onto the freeway.
为了回到高速公路上，前面会有一个非常糟糕的急转弯。

1221
00:50:43.370 --> 00:50:48.070
Mack has managed to get like all these police helicopters and a police escort so we can keep
麦克设法找来了所有这些警用直升机和警车护送，这样我们就能保持

1222
00:50:48.070 --> 00:50:49.530
the bus at 50 miles an hour.
巴士以每小时50英里的速度行驶。

1223
00:50:49.750 --> 00:50:50.690
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1224
00:50:50.890 --> 00:50:55.730
He's going to take them to this section of the 105 freeway that is under construction.
他要把他们带到105号高速公路正在施工的路段。

1225
00:50:55.730 --> 00:50:57.470
They're going to have complete control of it.
他们将完全掌控那里。

1226
00:50:57.570 --> 00:50:59.110
There's going to be like no traffic.
那里几乎没有交通。

1227
00:50:59.330 --> 00:51:00.470
It's going to be great.
那会很棒。

1228
00:51:00.470 --> 00:51:03.710
But in order to get there, you're going to have to take a super hard right.
但为了到达那里，你必须来一个超级急转弯。

1229
00:51:03.870 --> 00:51:05.410
A 90 degree turn.
一个90度的转弯。

1230
00:51:05.850 --> 00:51:06.890
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1231
00:51:07.590 --> 00:51:13.610
While all this is happening, Harry is starting to piece together who Howard Payne might be.
在这一切发生的同时，哈里开始拼凑出霍华德·佩恩可能是谁。

1232
00:51:14.070 --> 00:51:14.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1233
00:51:14.710 --> 00:51:18.490
Doing some just incredible think acting.
进行了一些令人难以置信的思考表演。

1234
00:51:18.890 --> 00:51:19.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1235
00:51:19.270 --> 00:51:19.890
He's got to look.
他得看。

1236
00:51:19.970 --> 00:51:20.690
He's got to get an idea.
他得有个头绪。

1237
00:51:20.770 --> 00:51:21.770
He's got to look at a computer.
他得看电脑。

1238
00:51:21.970 --> 00:51:23.530
He's got to look at a bulletin board.
他得看公告栏。

1239
00:51:23.730 --> 00:51:24.990
Lots of little glances.
很多细微的眼神交流。

1240
00:51:25.490 --> 00:51:25.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1241
00:51:25.850 --> 00:51:27.390
This is called glance acting.
这叫眼神表演。

1242
00:51:27.630 --> 00:51:30.210
I mean, I was riveted and I'm not even kidding.
我是说，我被深深吸引住了，我没开玩笑。

1243
00:51:30.410 --> 00:51:30.870
I know.
我知道。

1244
00:51:31.150 --> 00:51:32.350
So here's something.
所以这里有个情况。

1245
00:51:32.610 --> 00:51:37.630
The 105 freeway was actually under construction while they were filming this movie.
105号高速公路在拍摄这部电影时确实正在施工。

1246
00:51:37.950 --> 00:51:40.770
They got permission to shoot on the empty freeway.
他们获得了在空旷的高速公路上拍摄的许可。

1247
00:51:41.070 --> 00:51:45.890
But every day they would get like a report over which section of the freeway they were
但他们每天都会收到一份报告，说明他们被允许在高速公路的哪一段

1248
00:51:45.890 --> 00:51:46.530
allowed to shoot.
进行拍摄。

1249
00:51:46.610 --> 00:51:50.530
So they were having to move around because they were actively building it.
所以他们不得不四处移动，因为那里正在进行实际施工。

1250
00:51:50.770 --> 00:51:50.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1251
00:51:50.830 --> 00:51:55.810
Sometimes they would show up and there would be no lines painted and they would have to
有时候他们赶到现场，发现还没画好车道线，他们就不得不

1252
00:51:55.810 --> 00:51:58.730
paint lines on the freeway before they could start shooting.
在开拍前先在高速公路上画线。

1253
00:51:59.290 --> 00:51:59.430
Okay.
好吧。

1254
00:51:59.550 --> 00:52:01.330
I have to share with you what Jan said.
我得跟你们分享一下简说了什么。

1255
00:52:01.670 --> 00:52:05.690
I mean, I'm calling him Jan like we're best friends, but I listened to him talk for two
我是说，我叫他简，好像我们是好朋友一样，但我听他讲了两个

1256
00:52:05.690 --> 00:52:06.490
hours, you guys.
