00:58:56.540 --> 00:59:01.560
And I started driving up this ramp and I got all the physical symptoms of a panic attack.
我开始驶上这条匝道，然后就出现了惊恐发作的所有生理症状。

1420
00:59:01.800 --> 00:59:02.860
My heart started racing.
我的心跳开始加速。

1421
00:59:03.120 --> 00:59:04.520
Now, was this just on your own?
当时是你一个人吗？

1422
00:59:04.600 --> 00:59:05.320
Not from the movie?
不是因为电影情节？

1423
00:59:05.560 --> 00:59:06.360
Not from the movie.
不是因为电影。

1424
00:59:06.360 --> 00:59:08.860
This was just a moment that I had.
那纯粹是我个人的经历。

1425
00:59:09.080 --> 00:59:11.660
This ramp is very high up in the air.
这条匝道架得非常高。

1426
00:59:11.660 --> 00:59:14.560
I want you to know in real life, you go up very high.
我想告诉你们，在现实生活中，你得开到很高的地方。

1427
00:59:14.680 --> 00:59:16.520
It feels like you're going to go into the clouds.
感觉就像要冲进云端一样。

1428
00:59:17.060 --> 00:59:20.600
And the first time I drove it, I don't know what happened to me.
第一次开车经过时，我也不知道自己怎么了。

1429
00:59:20.740 --> 00:59:24.400
I went up the ramp and I started getting heart palpitations.
我开上匝道，就开始心悸。

1430
00:59:24.500 --> 00:59:25.460
My palms were sweating.
手心直冒汗。

1431
00:59:25.680 --> 00:59:27.540
I started getting shortness of breath.
开始呼吸困难。

1432
00:59:27.700 --> 00:59:30.740
I was in the throes of a panic attack.
我陷入了惊恐发作的折磨中。

1433
00:59:30.740 --> 00:59:35.000
I used all of my anxiety training to talk myself down.
我用尽了所有的焦虑应对训练来安抚自己。

1434
00:59:35.000 --> 00:59:39.200
I got off on the other side of the ramp and then it started to disperse.
我从匝道的另一头开了下去，那种感觉才开始消散。

1435
00:59:39.340 --> 00:59:42.880
But like I had to actually stop the car and take some deep breaths once I was off the ramp.
但下了匝道后，我确实不得不把车停下来，深呼吸了几次。

1436
00:59:43.240 --> 00:59:45.080
Just personal story about me and this ramp.
这只是我和这条匝道之间的一段个人往事。

1437
00:59:45.300 --> 00:59:47.040
Did you pull over on the side of the ramp?
你当时把车停在匝道边上了吗？

1438
00:59:47.280 --> 00:59:48.200
No, my God, no.
不，天哪，当然没有。

1439
00:59:48.320 --> 00:59:49.520
I had to get down the ramp.
我必须得先开下匝道。

1440
00:59:49.720 --> 00:59:50.580
Don't ever do that.
千万别那么做。

1441
00:59:50.740 --> 00:59:51.320
Never do that.
绝对不要。

1442
00:59:51.400 --> 00:59:51.600
No.
没。

1443
00:59:51.740 --> 00:59:53.240
I'm saying once I got off the ramp.
我是说等我下了匝道之后。

1444
00:59:53.240 --> 00:59:54.140
Once you were off the ramp.
等你下了匝道之后。

1445
00:59:54.140 --> 00:59:55.060
I took an exit.
我找了个出口开出去了。

1446
00:59:55.340 --> 00:59:56.520
And then you took a moment.
然后你缓了一会儿。

1447
00:59:56.880 --> 00:59:57.160
Huh.
呵。

1448
00:59:57.380 --> 00:59:59.000
I remember it like it was yesterday.
我记得清清楚楚，就像昨天发生的一样。

1449
00:59:59.000 --> 01:00:00.580
It was years and years and years ago.
那已经是很多很多年前的事了。

1450
01:00:00.580 --> 01:00:03.980
But anyway, this is a scary ramp, okay?
总之，这条匝道很吓人，明白吗？

1451
01:00:04.280 --> 01:00:05.040
It's a scary ramp.
这斜坡真吓人。

1452
01:00:05.160 --> 01:00:06.360
Even when it's completed.
即便是在完工之后。

1453
01:00:06.440 --> 01:00:07.940
This is what you need to know.
这是你需要了解的情况。

1454
01:00:08.940 --> 01:00:13.400
So something you should know is that there was no road missing in real life.
所以你该知道的是，现实中并没有那段缺失的路。

1455
01:00:13.540 --> 01:00:20.760
And in fact, at one hour and five minutes and 24 seconds in the establishing shot in the movie of this missing piece of road,
事实上，在电影中那个展示缺失路段的远景镜头里，时间在1小时5分24秒处，

1456
01:00:20.760 --> 01:00:28.200
they digitally removed the road, but you can still see the shadow from where the road would have been underneath.
他们用数字技术移除了那段路，但你依然能看到路面下方本该有的阴影。

1457
01:00:28.320 --> 01:00:31.440
So they forgot to digitally remove the shadow.
所以他们忘了把阴影也一并处理掉。

1458
01:00:31.700 --> 01:00:32.480
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1459
01:00:32.660 --> 01:00:33.020
Look at me.
看看我。

1460
01:00:33.180 --> 01:00:34.040
I'm like, oh, gosh.
我表现得好像，天哪。

1461
01:00:34.220 --> 01:00:38.760
Like, I know anything about, like, digital whatever.
就好像我懂什么数字特效之类的东西一样。

1462
01:00:39.060 --> 01:00:39.400
Yes.
没错。

1463
01:00:39.580 --> 01:00:42.080
Like, I'm like the shock, the horror, the shadow.
我表现得好像很震惊、很恐怖，还有那个阴影。

1464
01:00:42.840 --> 01:00:47.020
The writer said that the bus jump was not in the earlier drafts of the movie.
编剧说，巴士飞跃的桥段在电影的早期剧本中并没有出现。

1465
01:00:47.020 --> 01:00:55.260
He said this was Jan's idea, that Jan said, at a certain point in the movie, I want to hit a metaphorical wall.
他说这是简的主意，简当时说，在电影的某个节点，我想让主角撞上一堵隐喻的墙。

1466
01:00:55.440 --> 01:01:00.940
I want there to be a point where it looks like it's game over and there is no way they can get out of it.
我希望有一个时刻，看起来一切都完了，他们根本无法脱身。

1467
01:01:01.160 --> 01:01:05.960
He goes on to say that he thought at this point in the movie, the bus needed a really big challenge.
他接着说，他认为在电影的这个节点，巴士需要一个非常大的挑战。

1468
01:01:06.420 --> 01:01:10.060
And every day they were looking at parts of an unfinished freeway.
而他们每天都能看到一些未完工的高速公路路段。

1469
01:01:10.200 --> 01:01:14.580
So he asked the writers to write in the movie that there would be an unfinished bridge.
于是他要求编剧在电影里写进一段未完工的桥梁。

1470
01:01:14.580 --> 01:01:17.660
The studio told the director they thought this was ridiculous.
制片厂告诉导演，他们觉得这太荒谬了。

1471
01:01:17.980 --> 01:01:19.680
They said a bus can't jump a bridge.
他们说巴士不可能飞跃桥梁。

1472
01:01:19.840 --> 01:01:22.180
But the director fought really hard for this moment.
但导演为了这个镜头据理力争。

1473
01:01:22.400 --> 01:01:32.740
He said, listen, we need a big climactic moment for this bus and a big emotional moment where everyone is terrified and then they feel like relief and victory almoSt.
他说，听着，我们需要为这辆巴士安排一个高潮时刻，一个充满情感的时刻，让所有人都感到恐惧，然后又感到如释重负和近乎胜利的喜悦。

1474
01:01:33.240 --> 01:01:37.220
Now, to do this in real life, like we said, they stripped down the bus.
现在，为了在现实中实现这一点，正如我们所说，他们拆解了巴士。

1475
01:01:37.320 --> 01:01:38.740
They made it super duper light.
他们把它做得超级轻。

1476
01:01:38.980 --> 01:01:42.580
And they had stunt driver Joffrey Brown do this jump for real.
他们还请了特技车手杰弗里·布朗来实地完成这次飞跃。

1477
01:01:42.720 --> 01:01:43.740
He was driving the bus.
是他驾驶的巴士。

1478
01:01:43.840 --> 01:01:46.060
Not over a 50-foot gap, we should say.
我们得说明一下，并不是飞跃50英尺的缺口。

1479
01:01:46.300 --> 01:01:54.280
But they were going to have him drive 70 miles an hour up a ramp and then sort of launch off this ramp and land on the other side of this ramp.
但他们打算让他以时速70英里冲上斜坡，然后从斜坡上腾空而起，落在斜坡的另一侧。

1480
01:01:54.280 --> 01:02:03.080
And their biggest concern was that when the bus hit the ground, that that pressure would compress his spine and maybe break his spine.
他们最担心的是，当巴士撞击地面时，那股压力会压缩他的脊椎，甚至可能导致脊椎断裂。

1481
01:02:03.640 --> 01:02:15.080
So the stunt coordinator designed a special suspension safety harness to keep this from happening so that when the bus landed, he would be in like this like safety thing.
所以特技协调员设计了一种特殊的悬挂安全带，以防止这种情况发生，这样当巴士着陆时，他就会处于这种安全装置的保护中。

1482
01:02:15.260 --> 01:02:16.300
I'm doing the motion.
我正在做动作。

1483
01:02:16.300 --> 01:02:17.460
No one can see me.
没人能看见我。

1484
01:02:17.600 --> 01:02:18.300
I can see it.
我能看见。

1485
01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:19.460
You see what I'm doing.
你明白我在做什么。

1486
01:02:19.820 --> 01:02:20.380
It's selling it.
这很有说服力。

1487
01:02:20.480 --> 01:02:20.980
Thank you.
谢谢。

1488
01:02:20.980 --> 01:02:29.740
But then the other thing that they were concerned about was that they had some cameras that they were afraid might snap off their rigs and crush the driver.
但他们担心的另一件事是，有些摄像机可能会从支架上脱落并砸伤驾驶员。

1489
01:02:29.900 --> 01:02:32.380
But they rehearsed this for two weeks.
但他们为此排练了两周。

1490
01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:32.880
They did.
他们确实做了。

1491
01:02:33.160 --> 01:02:40.820
They also put Joffrey, the driver, in the middle of the bus in like this cage, like you said, with this suspension bungee thing.
他们还把驾驶员杰弗里安置在巴士中间的一个笼子里，就像你说的，配有那种悬挂式蹦极装置。

1492
01:02:41.240 --> 01:02:46.260
Because that way, if the bus compressed in the front or the back, he would be in the center of it.
因为这样一来，如果巴士的前部或后部受到挤压，他依然处于中心位置。

1493
01:02:46.260 --> 01:02:51.880
But they also had super suspension shocks on the bus to absorb some of that as well.
而且巴士上还装有超级悬挂减震器，也能吸收一部分冲击力。

1494
01:02:52.360 --> 01:02:53.860
And here's what Jan said.
简是这么说的。

1495
01:02:54.060 --> 01:03:02.160
He said the effects people told him that the bus would only go about 30 feet max because the bus was just too big to jump any further than that.
他说特效团队告诉他，巴士最多只能飞出30英尺，因为巴士太大了，跳不了那么远。

1496
01:03:02.280 --> 01:03:05.480
So he set his cameras up with that measurement in mind.
所以他根据这个测量结果架设了摄像机。

1497
01:03:05.680 --> 01:03:06.880
And there were like a ton.
而且当时架了好多台。

1498
01:03:06.880 --> 01:03:07.560
Yeah.
没错。

1499
01:03:07.800 --> 01:03:16.000
And then in reality, the bus actually flew over all of his cameras and landed on two of them, totally destroying one of them.
结果实际上，巴士直接飞过了他所有的摄像机，还砸坏了其中两台，彻底报废了一台。

1500
01:03:16.160 --> 01:03:21.820
He said thankfully he had put one camera 90 feet out because that's the one that caught the landing.
他说幸好他把一台摄像机放在了90英尺外，因为正是那台摄像机拍到了着陆的画面。

1501
01:03:22.300 --> 01:03:25.340
They could not believe how far this bus actually flew.
他们简直不敢相信这辆巴士竟然飞出了那么远。

1502
01:03:25.600 --> 01:03:28.940
At its highest point, the front of it was 20 feet in the air.
在最高点时，车头离地有20英尺高。

1503
01:03:29.120 --> 01:03:30.600
It actually went out of frame.
它甚至飞出了画面。

1504
01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:32.340
You can see that in the movie.
你在电影里能看到这一点。

1505
01:03:32.500 --> 01:03:32.660
Yeah.
没错。

1506
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:33.300
Yes.
是的。

1507
01:03:33.380 --> 01:03:36.080
It went far more vertical than they expected.
它比他们预想的要垂直得多。

1508
01:03:36.920 --> 01:03:41.900
And in reality, the bus stayed in the air for 0.49 seconds.
实际上，巴士在空中只停留了0.49秒。

1509
01:03:42.100 --> 01:03:50.640
But because they had all of these cameras and then they kind of slowed down the speed of the film, it stays in the air for 11 seconds in the movie.
但因为他们布置了这么多摄像机，又调慢了胶片的播放速度，所以电影里它在空中停留了11秒。

1510
01:03:51.160 --> 01:03:55.940
Jan went on to say he really wanted to be able to show the passengers of the bus reacting to the landing.
简接着说，他真的很想展现出乘客对落地瞬间的反应。

1511
01:03:56.540 --> 01:04:01.440
So they actually got another bus and rigged it to do a very, very small jump.
于是他们找来了另一辆巴士，改装后让它做了一个非常非常小的跳跃。

1512
01:04:01.440 --> 01:04:11.940
He said it only went about eight inches in the air, but the actors had real reactions because even just eight inches, that's a big impact for a structure as big as a bus.
他说这辆车只离地跳了约八英寸，但演员们的反应是真实的，因为即使只有八英寸，对于像巴士这么大的结构来说，冲击力也是很大的。

1513
01:04:12.240 --> 01:04:13.640
And they said it was fun.
他们说这很有趣。

1514
01:04:13.700 --> 01:04:14.740
It felt like a roller coaster.
感觉就像坐过山车一样。

1515
01:04:15.060 --> 01:04:15.300
Wow.
哇。

1516
01:04:15.800 --> 01:04:21.140
One other thing, Jan, you know, he had sort of said in the beginning, listen, we had cameras everywhere.
还有一件事，简，你知道，他起初说过，听着，我们到处都架设了摄像机。

1517
01:04:22.020 --> 01:04:23.300
We had pulleys.
我们有滑轮组。

1518
01:04:23.940 --> 01:04:25.900
We had all of these rigs.
我们有各种各样的装置。

1519
01:04:25.980 --> 01:04:30.360
It was impossible when we edited to sometimes not capture another camera.
剪辑的时候，有时根本无法避免拍到其他的摄像机。

1520
01:04:30.540 --> 01:04:30.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1521
01:04:31.200 --> 01:04:34.420
So I did do a pass called Spot That Camera.
所以我做了一个名为“寻找摄像机”的剪辑。

1522
01:04:34.760 --> 01:04:35.040
Okay.
好的。

1523
01:04:35.420 --> 01:04:36.280
There are so many.
里面有太多了。

1524
01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:37.260
Really?
真的吗？

1525
01:04:37.380 --> 01:04:38.000
There are so many.
真的有好多。

1526
01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:42.280
There's one on the side of the road on a tripod, like a big camera.
路边有一个架在三脚架上的，那种大摄像机。

1527
01:04:42.980 --> 01:04:44.580
There's ones on the side of the bus.
巴士侧面也有。

1528
01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:46.880
They try to make them kind of look like they're part of the bus.
他们试图让它们看起来像是巴士的一部分。

1529
01:04:46.920 --> 01:04:50.500
But like, I mean, listen, I'm sure you guys don't want to do this.
但说真的，听着，我肯定你们不想这么做。

1530
01:04:50.580 --> 01:04:53.380
You don't want to watch speed just trying to look for cameras.
你们不会想看《生死时速》时专门去盯着找摄像机。

1531
01:04:53.520 --> 01:04:54.520
But there were a lot.
但确实有很多。

1532
01:04:54.700 --> 01:04:55.160
You could.
你可以试试。

1533
01:04:55.320 --> 01:04:55.760
You could.
你可以试试。

1534
01:04:56.060 --> 01:05:03.720
Well, they do their jump, and now they are headed to the airport, which is going to be great because they're going to be able to control things now.
好吧，他们完成了跳跃，现在正前往机场，这太棒了，因为他们现在可以控制局面了。

1535
01:05:03.980 --> 01:05:06.680
And the bus can just drive in a giant circle.
巴士可以绕着巨大的圆圈行驶。

1536
01:05:06.680 --> 01:05:10.960
Well, in the original script, the bus was going to circle Dodger Stadium.
其实在最初的剧本里，巴士是要绕着道奇体育场转圈的。

1537
01:05:11.380 --> 01:05:15.600
And then it was going to go on, and it was going to blow up by the Hollywood sign.
然后它会继续行驶，并在好莱坞标志牌附近爆炸。

1538
01:05:16.220 --> 01:05:24.120
The writer, Graham, said that he actually looked at like an overview of Los Angeles, and he was like, where can a bus go in a circle?
编剧格雷厄姆说，他当时看了洛杉矶的概览图，心想，哪里有能让巴士绕圈的地方呢？

1539
01:05:24.720 --> 01:05:27.220
And he saw the parking lot at Dodger Stadium.
然后他看到了道奇体育场的停车场。

1540
01:05:27.500 --> 01:05:31.400
But the O'Malley's who owned Dodger Stadium at the time were not into it.
但当时拥有道奇体育场的奥马利家族并不乐意。

1541
01:05:31.400 --> 01:05:32.140
They weren't into it.
他们不感兴趣。

1542
01:05:32.180 --> 01:05:32.940
They weren't having it.
他们根本不答应。

1543
01:05:33.020 --> 01:05:33.700
They said no.
他们拒绝了。

1544
01:05:33.700 --> 01:05:43.580
So they changed it to the airport, which was actually really helpful because then as a story point, they could restrict all the, you know, the news cameras.
所以他们改成了机场，这其实非常有帮助，因为作为一个剧情点，他们可以限制所有的，你知道，新闻摄像机。

1545
01:05:43.880 --> 01:05:44.700
Yeah, the airspace.
没错，还有领空。

1546
01:05:45.120 --> 01:05:45.800
It worked great.
效果非常好。

1547
01:05:46.120 --> 01:05:52.440
Jack's going to get a phone call because the bomber has a cell phone now, his giant AT&T big handheld cell phone.
杰克要接到电话了，因为炸弹客现在有手机了，就是他那个巨大的AT&T手持大哥大。

1548
01:05:52.580 --> 01:05:58.080
Can we talk about his choice to hold the cell phone across his body?
我们能聊聊他为什么选择横跨身体拿着手机吗？

1549
01:05:58.280 --> 01:05:59.160
Oh, Dennis Hopper.
哦，丹尼斯·霍珀。

1550
01:05:59.160 --> 01:06:06.320
Yeah, so Dennis Hopper is holding it in his right hand, which is his undamaged hand.
对，丹尼斯·霍珀是用右手拿着它的，那是他没受伤的那只手。

1551
01:06:06.420 --> 01:06:11.460
You know, his one hand, he lost his thumb in some sort of incident at work.
你知道，他的一只手，他在工作中因为某种事故失去了大拇指。

1552
01:06:11.600 --> 01:06:11.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1553
01:06:12.400 --> 01:06:17.120
So he's holding the phone with his other hand, but then he crosses it over to his left ear.
所以他用另一只手拿着电话，但随后他把它换到了左耳边。

1554
